<LanguageData>
  <!--EN: This person does not suffer fatal hypothermia. Instead, their bodies gradually slow down and enter a dormant state when exposed to extreme cold, and they can awaken safely once warmed.-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.description>此人没有遭受致命的低温症。相反，当暴露极度寒冷时，他们的身体会逐渐减慢并进入休眠状态，一旦变暖，他们就可以安全地醒来。</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.description>
  <!--EN: cryostasis-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.label>低温停滞</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.label>
  <!--EN: shivering-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.0.label>发抖</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.0.label>
  <!--EN: initial-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.1.label>最初的</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.1.label>
  <!--EN: drowsy-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.2.label>昏昏欲睡</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.2.label>
  <!--EN: sleep-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.3.label>睡觉</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.3.label>
  <!--EN: deep sleep-->
  <VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.4.label>深度睡眠</VREStarjack_CryostasisHediff.stages.4.label>
  <!--EN: This creature is suffering from oxygen toxicity caused by exposure to a breathable atmosphere. Their lungs cannot tolerate this much oxygen. They will die soon unless removed to a low-oxygen or vacuum environment.-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.description>这种生物因暴露在可呼吸的大气中而遭受氧中毒。他们的肺部无法承受这么多的氧气。除非转移到低氧或真空环境中，否则它们很快就会死亡。</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.description>
  <!--EN: hyperoxia-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.label>高氧</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.label>
  <!--EN: initial-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.0.label>最初的</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.0.label>
  <!--EN: initial-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.1.label>最初的</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.1.label>
  <!--EN: mild-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.2.label>温和的</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.2.label>
  <!--EN: moderate-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.3.label>缓和</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.3.label>
  <!--EN: extreme-->
  <VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.4.label>极端</VREStarjack_Hyperoxia.stages.4.label>
</LanguageData>
